@startuml class_diagram
' =============================================================================
' CAEGraph - Design UML (Class Diagram)
' =============================================================================
' PURPOSE : "Planned design" - the domain abstractions of CAEGraph.
' OWNER   : Architecture Agent
' RULES   :
'   - Update this diagram BEFORE implementing code.
'   - Show abstractions, responsibilities and relationships.
'   - Do NOT enumerate concrete method signatures; that is Generated UML's job.
' GUIDE   : see architecture/UML_GUIDE.md
' =============================================================================

title CAEGraph Domain Abstractions (Design) - ADR-007-024

package "external ecosystem bases" {
  class "torch_geometric.data.Data" as PyGData <<external>>
  abstract class "torch_geometric.data.Dataset" as PyGDataset <<external>>
  abstract class "torch.nn.Module" as TorchModule <<external>>
}

package "caegraph.core (domain truth: CAEGraph + topology subsystem; torch-only, never PyG)" {
  abstract class BaseObject {
    Base abstraction: identity, metadata, validation contract
  }
  class Registry {
    Name-keyed registry/factory for loaders and
    transforms (register / get / build);
    duplicate names rejected (Phase 1);
    name->factory only, callable check is the
    contract; runtime type enforcement
    (base_class + issubclass) recorded as a
    future option, deliberately not Phase 1;
    general utility registry only; domain
    registries are dedicated classes
  }
  class CAEGraph {
    Graph-native canonical domain
    representation (ADR-015).
    Semantic composition (ADR-018):
    entities, relations, geometry,
    fields, regions, conditions;
    topology subsystem is an optional
    semantic provider referenced by
    CAEGraph - present for cell-based,
    absent for mesh-free (ADR-014).
    Phase 2 minimal storage (dedicated
    authorization, ADR-019): construction-
    filled node graph relations, node-entity
    annotations and associated fields, with
    read-only accessors; n_entities = node
    graph vertex count (== n_nodes, NOT
    entity total). Domain entity identities
    are NOT duplicated here - referenced
    via Mesh node/cell indices (ADR-019 D1).
    Semantic composition does not
    define class members or storage
    layout. Never imports PyG -
    PyG / networkx / igraph are
    backends or analysis engines,
    never the domain model
  }
  note right of CAEGraph
    Temporal organization responsibilities
    (ADR-023 D-01/D-04/D-08): aggregate
    boundary for Snapshot lifecycle and
    organization; coordinates the single
    mutation / consistency boundary of
    membership; canonical temporal storage
    does not duplicate global/static
    realizations per Snapshot (D-08).
    Selection chain: explicit Snapshot
    temporal selection -> candidate
    single-state (all members + eligible
    global realizations) -> per-Field
    0/1/>1: 0 = declaration-only (ADR-022
    D-06 zero footprint); 1 = enters the
    final state directly; >1 = residual
    non-temporal multiplicity, explicit
    select or fail per ADR-020 D6 (never
    delegated to the adapter) -> final
    single-state projection: a NEW
    canonical CAEGraph representation,
    not a mutable view of the source
    (ADR-024 D-01); projection-formed
    state is free of mutable canonical
    alias to the source; sharing reserved
    for non-mutation-channel (immutable)
    state (ADR-024 D-02); selected
    Snapshot + snapshot-scoped FieldData
    independently materialized,
    exactly-one membership preserved
    (ADR-024 D-03, ADR-023 D-03);
    realization-independent canonical
    semantics preserved (ADR-024 D-04);
    mechanism (copy / COW /
    lazy-materialization / shared
    immutable substrate) unfrozen -
    narrows the ADR-023 D-08 deferred
    space only -> existing
    BackendAdapter unchanged (zero-selector).
    Validation: physical_time presence &
    uniqueness (D02-01), membership
    single-valued (D03-01), scope dichotomy
    (D04-01), per-Field scope exclusivity
    (D04-02) enforced at the CAEGraph-
    coordinated temporal write path
    (container form deferred, D-04);
    membership independence of timestep
    (D07-01) is a semantic guard test only.
  end note
  class Field {
    Stable physical quantity declaration
    (ADR-020 D1): name, unit, association,
    component semantics - the single
    authoritative source (D3);
    association REQUIRED - non-empty
    entity family, None illegal
    (ADR-021 D3);
    NO values, NO timestep; may legally
    exist without any FieldData
    (problem-before-solving, D4);
    semantic role only - exact
    member/API form not frozen
  }
  class FieldData <<"realization member">> {
    One realization of a Field
    (ADR-020 D2): values payload;
    semantic role only - exact
    member/API form not frozen;
    current Phase 2 implementation
    uses the field-split member set;
    supported realization families:
    node / cell - unsupported/typo
    rejected at construction
    (ADR-021 D5);
    explicit scope: global/static |
    snapshot-scoped (ADR-023 D-04) -
    never inferred from missing
    time information
  }
  note right of FieldData
    Realization metadata examples
    (illustrative, NOT frozen - ADR-020 D2):
    timestep / time / coverage /
    sample identity.
    Identity / reference mechanism
    deferred (ADR-020 D3): read-only
    proxy / cache / derived accessors
    all unfrozen.
    Lineage (BaseObject or not)
    deferred (ADR-020 scope exclusion).
    Lives in the CAEGraph canonical
    data flow, accessible via the
    canonical representation;
    ownership / container / storage
    NOT frozen (ADR-020 D4).
    FieldData.timestep (current member):
    legacy / compatibility member - NO
    canonical temporal authority;
    participates in no membership /
    ordering / alignment / selection;
    no defined mapping to physical_time
    or solver_step (ADR-023 D-07);
    long-term fate deferred.
  end note
  class Snapshot <<"temporal organization construct">> {
    Canonical realization organization
    construct (ADR-023 D-01): groups
    existing FieldData into one
    instantaneous physical state via
    explicit membership; adds realization
    temporal organization semantics only -
    NOT a new physical-domain concept
    category (no ADR-018 / ADR-007 count
    increase); temporal organization is
    optional - zero Snapshots legal (D-01);
    instantaneous-state descriptor - holds
    authoritative non-owning membership;
    no selection / projection service
    responsibilities (D-03/D-08)
    identity : snapshot structural identity
    physical_time : REQUIRED, unique within
    the temporal organization - sole
    global-ordering coordinate, non-uniform
    spacing legal (D-02/D-08)
    solver_step : optional provenance (D-02)
    (conceptual properties only - member
    names / types not frozen, D-02)
  }
  note right of Snapshot
    Membership descriptor (ADR-023
    D-03/D-04/D-06): this class holds the
    authoritative non-owning membership of
    its member FieldData; snapshot-scoped
    FieldData -> exactly 1 Snapshot;
    global/static realizations have no
    membership; scope never inferred from
    missing time information; per-Field
    scope mixing rejected (the single
    ADR-023 Phase 2 narrowing, D-04); no
    (Snapshot, Field) cardinality cap -
    multiple realizations of one Field in
    one Snapshot are legal residual
    non-temporal multiplicity, disambiguated
    at projection formation (D-05/D-08);
    empty Snapshot legal (D-06).
    Reverse access (FieldData -> Snapshot),
    if present, is derived only - no two
    independently-modifiable membership
    truth sources (D-03).
  end note
  enum BoundaryType {
    Mathematical BC categories (ADR-010):
    DIRICHLET / NEUMANN / ROBIN /
    PERIODIC / SYMMETRY / INTERFACE / NONE;
    software-specific names (wall, inlet...)
    live in BoundaryRegion metadata, never here.
    Single enum holds both constraint and
    role axes (ADR-011 Phase 2 freeze);
    orthogonal split deferred
  }
  enum NodeCategory {
    INTERIOR / BOUNDARY / CORNER
  }
  class BoundaryManager {
    Semantic region registry (ADR-018):
    name -> BoundaryRegion, spec binding
    by name resolution, corner
    (multi-region) queries; references
    topology, does not own it
  }
  class BoundaryRegion {
    Semantic region (ADR-018): membership
    is represented according to the
    source discretization; cell-based:
    dim == topo_dim - 1, membership =
    canonical topology identifiers
    (global facet IDs, node sets as
    derived views, ADR-014); references
    topology, does not own it; targetable
    by BoundarySpec by name; carries
    software naming metadata per
    ADR-010; BaseObject domain-truth family
  }
  class BoundarySpec {
    User-facing boundary declaration: type, value,
    weight, space/time dependence;
    paired_region slot for PERIODIC,
    generic parameters container for ROBIN
    (design slots, Phase 2 contract, ADR-010);
    per-type slot-coherence validation
    required, fail-fast (ADR-011)
  }
  abstract class FieldFunction {
    Callable analytic boundary/initial value:
    (t, pos) -> tensors, shape self-validation
  }

  package "topology (topology subsystem - optional semantic provider, first-class for cell-based discretizations, ADR-014/018)" {
    class Mesh {
      Topology-rich discretization
      representation (ADR-015): one
      cell-based topology representation
      supported by the topology subsystem
      (FEM/FVM); nodes (n,3) + topo_dim;
      cells CSR (int-coded cell_types /
      connectivity / offsets, single truth,
      type views derived only); explicit
      facets CSR + validated ragged
      facet_cells (winding-free); domain
      groups (plain global-cell-id data);
      structure frozen after validate
      (ADR-014)
    }
    enum CellType {
      LINE2 / TRI3 / QUAD4 / TET4 / PYR5 /
      WEDGE6 / HEX8 (POINT + higher-order =
      future); explicit stable integer codes,
      never enum-declaration order; dim,
      node_count, CAEGraph local-node
      convention + codim-1 face templates
      (frozen with implementation, ADR-014)
    }
  }
}

package "caegraph.geometry" {
  class GeometryProcessor {
    Geometric services: edge features
    (distance, direction, normal, quality),
    field interpolation
  }
}

package "caegraph.io" {
  abstract class AbstractMeshLoader {
    Cross-format loading pipeline
    (ADR-012): __call__(path) -> Mesh is
    stable; per-format protected hooks are
    implementation details, not frozen;
    parse source format, then produce
    topology input per ADR-014 (incl.
    explicit facets + validated
    facet-cell adjacency); source named
    groups classified by dim vs topo dim
    into domain / boundary-interface
    group metadata (ADR-012 - preserved
    for downstream region construction;
    lower-dim groups -> diagnostics);
    IO never infers BoundaryType - math
    categories come from user specs only
  }
  class GmshLoader {
    First concrete AbstractMeshLoader for gmsh
    source named groups via meshio
    (provisional engine, ADR-013; types
    never leak past io); performs the
    ADR-012 normalization obligations per
    ADR-014 (block-local ids, local-node
    convention, facet winding, group
    representation)
  }
  interface MeshWriter {
    Write-back into the CAE ecosystem;
    VTK / ParaView first
  }
}

package "caegraph.graph (representation construction + backend adapter)" {
  class MeshRepresentationBuilder {
    Phase 2 cell-based realization
    (ADR-016/019):
    domain entities: node entity family
    (ID = canonical Mesh node ID) +
    cell entity family (ID = canonical
    Mesh cell ID, identity via Mesh
    cell index, no independent storage
    - ADR-019 D1);
    Phase 2 node graph vertices =
    node entities (representation
    choice, not entity definition);
    relations = deduplicated (min, max)
    node pairs expanded from cell
    codim-1 faces (1D cells contribute
    their own node pair);
    NodeCategory derived from
    boundary-participation regions via
    mechanical mapping: 0 -> INTERIOR /
    1 -> BOUNDARY / >=2 -> CORNER;
    applicability limited to
    boundary-class regions, general
    region classification deferred
    (ADR-019 D4);
    construction-time validation
    (ADR-019 D5 as amended by ADR-020 D5):
    FieldData cardinality: leading entity
    axis == n_nodes (node) /
    n_cells (cell); fail-fast otherwise;
    unsupported realization families
    rejected (ADR-021 D5);
    region membership out-of-bounds ->
    construction failure;
    NodeCategory is a construction-time
    result; later manager mutation does
    not retroactively update it;
    construction is a strategy layer -
    further source families extend it
    per ADR-016 (no frozen hierarchy,
    registry or naming; replaces the
    single Mesh -> GraphBuilder
    contract, ADR-009)
  }
  class BackendAdapter {
    CAEGraph -> framework-specific
    graph representation;
    PyG Data is the Phase 2 form;
    DataGraph is a conceptual backend
    representation layer, not a required
    class, never the domain graph
    object (ADR-017); concrete
    interface not frozen;
    undirected CAEGraph relations may
    be materialized HERE as backend-
    specific symmetric directed pairs
    (u,v)/(v,u); this transformation
    belongs to backend representation,
    never CAEGraph storage (ADR-017/019);
    domain input (ADR-020 D4): the
    CAEGraph canonical representation
    ONLY - with optional FieldData
    accessible semantics; external
    field-value injection signatures
    are contract-excluded;
    declaration-only graphs yield no
    fabricated realization values;
    on gate 4b resumption: if
    materialization requires a unique
    realization and multiple eligible
    FieldData exist, explicitly select
    or fail (ADR-020 D6);
    temporal projection path (ADR-023 D-08,
    CAEGraph side) provides a single-state
    CAEGraph input; the adapter performs no
    temporal selection - ADR-022 D-05
    fail-fast preserved unchanged
  }
}

package "caegraph.transforms" {
  class GeometryTransform {
    Coordinate / feature normalization
  }
  class FeatureTransform {
    CAE feature engineering on
    backend graph representation
  }
  class PhysicsTransform {
    Boundary-condition encoding:
    data.x[data.inlet_mask] = value pattern
    (BC application lives HERE,
    not on the domain object)
  }
}

package "caegraph.dataset" {
  class CAEDataset {
    Collections, transforms, splits;
    backend-specific (ADR-009)
  }
}

package "caegraph.physics" {
  class PhysicsLoss {
    PDE residuals / physics-informed loss terms
  }
}

package "caegraph.models (interface + utilities, no GNN zoo)" {
  abstract class Model {
    GNN model abstraction:
    encode - process - decode contract;
    backend-specific (ADR-009);
    concrete architectures (MeshGraphNet/GNO/...)
    live in examples / external projects (ADR-008)
  }
}

package "caegraph.assimilation" {
  class Observation {
    Observation operators: sparse measurements
    (e.g. PIV) on graph fields
  }
  class Correction {
    Correction operators: dense prediction +
    observation -> improved field
  }
}

package "caegraph.workflow (training utilities, no fit loop)" {
  class LossAssembly {
    Compose data + physics + observation
    loss terms (consumes assimilation, physics)
  }
  class BatchAdaptation {
    CAE-aware batching helpers
  }
}

package "caegraph.inference (neural simulation harness)" {
  class Simulator {
    CAEGraph (any discretization) +
    pretrained model -> fields;
    backend data -> forward ->
    field reconstruction
  }
  class Rollout {
    Transient rollout LOOP harness;
    numerical schemes stay model-side (ADR-007 D5)
  }
}

' --- Relationships -----------------------------------------------------------

BaseObject <|-- CAEGraph
BaseObject <|-- Mesh
BaseObject <|-- Field
BaseObject <|-- BoundaryRegion
AbstractMeshLoader <|-- GmshLoader

CAEDataset ..> PyGDataset : Phase 2 implementation binding (ADR-009)
Model ..> TorchModule : Phase 2 implementation binding (ADR-009)

BoundaryManager "1" o-- "*" BoundaryRegion : registers
BoundaryManager "1" o-- "*" BoundarySpec : binds
BoundarySpec --> BoundaryType : typed by
BoundarySpec "*" --> "0..1" BoundaryRegion : targets by name
BoundarySpec "*" o--> "0..1" FieldFunction : optional value
Field "1" <-- "0..*" FieldData : corresponds to declaration / Field is semantic authoritative source (identity/reference mechanism deferred - ADR-020 D3)
CAEGraph ..> Field : associated quantity declarations (ADR-020 D1/D4)
CAEGraph ..> FieldData : canonical data flow access - ownership / container / storage deferred (ADR-020 D4)
CAEGraph "1" --> "0..*" Snapshot : temporal organization - aggregate boundary (lifecycle & organization); zero Snapshots legal; storage / container form deferred (ADR-023 D-01/D-04)
Snapshot "0..1" --> "0..*" FieldData : authoritative non-owning membership - snapshot-scoped FieldData -> exactly 1 instantaneous state (0 = global/static); reverse access derived only; mutation / consistency coordinated by CAEGraph temporal responsibility (ADR-023 D-03/D-04)
CAEGraph ..> Mesh : cell-based topology example (optional semantic provider; ADR-014/018)
CAEGraph ..> BoundaryManager : uses semantic regions
CAEGraph ..> NodeCategory : node-entity annotation only (Phase 2; cell entities excluded - ADR-019 D3)
BoundaryRegion ..> Mesh : references facet namespace (cell-based; does not own topology)

AbstractMeshLoader ..> Mesh : produces topology input
MeshWriter ..> Mesh : consumes
MeshRepresentationBuilder ..> Mesh : cell-based source example (ADR-016)
MeshRepresentationBuilder ..> GeometryProcessor : future geometry feature integration (deferred - ADR-019 not-covered items)
MeshRepresentationBuilder ..> CAEGraph : produces
MeshRepresentationBuilder ..> BoundaryManager : consumes explicit region ownership (ADR-019 D5)
BackendAdapter ..> CAEGraph : consumes
BackendAdapter ..> PyGData : Phase 2 backend example (produces)
GeometryTransform ..> PyGData : operates on
FeatureTransform ..> PyGData : operates on
PhysicsTransform ..> PyGData : operates on
CAEDataset ..> PyGData : consumes (Phase 2)
Model ..> PhysicsLoss : may consume
CAEDataset "1" --> "*" Model : provides data for

LossAssembly ..> PhysicsLoss : composes
LossAssembly ..> Observation : composes (training-constraint mode)
Rollout ..> Model : calls
Simulator ..> Rollout : orchestrates
Simulator ..> MeshWriter : exports results
Correction ..> Observation : uses (post-inference mode)

note right of BackendAdapter
  Positioning (ADR-008, clarified by
  ADR-015/017): no solver abstraction,
  no trainer abstraction; backend
  adapters are allowed - backend
  replacement requires architecture
  review confirming the CAEGraph
  domain boundary and dependency
  direction remain unchanged (ADR-017).
end note

@enduml
